        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@da-woods Did you get a chance to look at my previous comment? \n\nRegarding your previous reply, I am less concerned about whether the path would exist or not and more about reproducibility of builds. The current situation causes a different cpp file to be generated from the same cython source file if you just change the directory where cythonize was invoked from. This causes misses in ccache and also breaks our deployment workflow which uses md5 hashes to determine whether an artifact needs to be deployed or not.\n\nI also think that the problem here is not about deciding what is the right thing to do. This clearly looks like a bug to me because the code itself contradicts what the comment right above it says.",
